From 5e822abba84554ddba0826239b46ca3fb2aa5623 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:44:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): machine files for the other Tormach mills;
 belt ranges and rigid tapping from the .mch

Ships inch machine files for the Tormach 770MX (ML), 770M, 1100MX,
1500MX and PCNC 440, each from its own Tormach operator's manual
(UM10864, UM10539, UM10586, UM10811, UM10372), next to the 770MX (MF,
UM10587) from #131.

The .mch spindle gains two optional fields:
- `ranges` (the hand-changed belt ranges), read by the Tormach post's
  belt note as `machine.spindleRanges` in place of the 770 family's
  hard-coded numbers. A one-range machine gets no note.
- `rigid_tapping`, which the post reads as `machine.rigidTapping`. It
  is false on the R8 mills (770M, PCNC 440), where the post refuses a
  tap cycle by name instead of writing G84.

Unstated, both read as before for every other machine. The generic-VMC
synth golden loses its 770-family belt comment.

Not shipped: the non-MX 1100 and the plain 770 (no manual in hand).

Refs #170

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
